WEBVTT

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:43.180
I'm sure... I hid it here.

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:47.980
There it is!

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:51.130
My emergency survival bread...

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:54.490
I-I over-treasured it.

00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:56.860
It's gotten moldy...

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:02.420
Payday is still...

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:04.100
Umm...

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.430
I'll be counting on you from now on.

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:13.740
Leave it to me.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.710
A party...

00:02:19.190 --> 00:02:21.460
Please, do drop by.

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:26.840
It's an invitation to a bal masqué,

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:29.460
combined with the publication of <i>that</i> research.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:36.300
That's way too soon.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:52.850
I wonder who was talking to the principal.

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:57.760
More importantly, if there's a party, there will be food...

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:36.050
Bull's eye!

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:45.500
Komurasaki-kun!

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:02.360
I'm relieved.

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:03.910
Himawari-san.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:06.730
You'll be fine after resting for a couple of days.

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:07.990
Thank you.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:15.390
E-Everyone!

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:18.900
Even so, where from?

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:22.570
I escaped from their hideout.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:27.800
All boys are held captive there after they were drugged,

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:31.450
and have ultimately become the subjects of their experiments.

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:33.240
Don't stress yourself!

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:34.530
The subjects of their experiments...

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:37.560
Are you talking about those modified ninjas?

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:39.710
They're already here?

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:43.680
The gum-crazy and the leafy one, the one who transforms at the sight of okonomiyaki,

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:46.500
and one who sneaks into other people's hearts.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:48.200
Geez, they were such a hassle.

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:52.460
I couldn't rescue anyone from there.

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:54.200
It took me all I have to escape from them.

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:57.940
Nanafushi was the only one spared from the attack.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:00.270
Really?! Is he all right? That's great!

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:02.210
Where is their hideout?

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:08.460
Maybe because of the construction of the building, but my balance was off.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:12.570
Thus I had no sense of direction and don't remember my escape route.

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:13.760
The only clue is...

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:17.170
That's...

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:21.590
It probably stuck to Komurasaki's clothes during his escape.

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:23.980
It's the fruit of a poisonous blue magnolia.

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:30.230
It's only natural habitat is the swampy land at the borders of the Village of the Mist.

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:33.080
Looks like it's my turn.

00:05:34.130 --> 00:05:35.880
009-1.

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:38.060
It means kunoichi.

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:41.230
Note: "9" is usually read as "kyuu," but sometimes "ku." The dash is read as "no," and "1" reads "ichi."

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:41.230
I will contact you once I get into their hideout.

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:42.450
This is the receiver.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:45.480
The Kunoichi Spy's Great Strategy commences!

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:45.980
Bye!

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:50.090
Hey, don't push on me!

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:51.460
Move over there!

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:54.540
I-I'm sorry, Komurasaki-kun.

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:56.650
No, I don't mind.

00:05:56.650 --> 00:05:58.470
Rather, move closer...

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:16.680
Looks like it's going smoothly.

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:18.400
Yes.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:20.690
It's almost going too smoothly.

00:06:46.730 --> 00:06:48.600
009-1 here.

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:49.320
Respond.

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:51.170
She's there.

00:06:51.170 --> 00:06:53.820
Himeji here. We can hear you loud and clear.

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:56.880
I've found their hideout.

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:59.830
Looks like there's going to be a party,

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:02.440
but everyone's masquerading.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:04.390
It's as if they aren't willing to expose their identity.

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:06.310
They're suspicious.

00:07:06.310 --> 00:07:08.570
Anyway, I am going to infiltrate.

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:56.380
I'm back, I've just successfully infiltrated the security room.

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:00.130
Show me your invitation card.

00:08:00.770 --> 00:08:02.720
How rude!

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:04.500
Here it is.

00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:08.800
My apologies.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:10.870
Please, put this on.

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:16.110
I'm going to stuff myself!

00:08:21.510 --> 00:08:24.030
It's easy to sneak in from the sides of the gates.

00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:26.880
I wonder where the windows are.

00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:30.040
Well. I will continue surveying.

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:31.390
Got it.

00:08:40.170 --> 00:08:41.450
Azami-chan!

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:49.280
Delicious!

00:08:55.490 --> 00:08:56.850
Amazing!

00:08:57.450 --> 00:08:59.950
You can even pierce steel walls.

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:01.940
That's wonderful, Yusura-chan.

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:04.510
It's a present from Yonezawa-kun.

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:06.800
Its tip is made of kongouseki.

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:07.850
What's kongouseki?

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:09.680
Diamond.

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:12.820
You got diamonds in exchange for the cucumbers?

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:15.150
It can also cut glass windows with ease.

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:16.640
Let's go, Momota.

00:09:25.150 --> 00:09:28.650
All the security guards are gathered here.

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:30.880
Is this all?

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:34.440
Don't overlook any intruders.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:35.650
Go now if you understand.

00:09:36.190 --> 00:09:37.280
Yes, sir.

00:09:40.150 --> 00:09:42.120
J-Just that?

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:46.400
What's the use of gathering all of us here now?

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:49.910
Hey, don't speak so recklessly.

00:09:49.910 --> 00:09:53.670
After all he is the most important consultant for this project.

00:09:54.430 --> 00:09:56.310
Everyone, back to your positions!

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:03.670
What a strange building.

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:06.410
I wonder where on earth Azami-chan is.

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:09.850
Momota, let us know once you've found a trace of Azami-chan's scent.

00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:15.820
Hurry!

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:23.600
In here, Momota?

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:25.340
There's no door knob.

00:10:25.340 --> 00:10:27.110
We should just break through it.

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:30.590
This is...

00:10:31.350 --> 00:10:33.490
Please input password.

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:35.010
Password?

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:36.050
Do you have an idea?

00:10:36.050 --> 00:10:37.410
Like I know it.

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:45.520
Please input the correct password.

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:47.060
It's no use.

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:49.390
I tried with my date of birth.

00:10:49.390 --> 00:10:51.040
There's no meaning to that.

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:54.200
Then, how about Yonezawa-kun's?

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:58.430
Usually it's forbidden to use dates of birth and telephone numbers.

00:10:58.650 --> 00:11:02.400
Then how about the anniversary of me meeting Yonezawa-kun?

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:05.810
Could it be 009-1?

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:14.970
I figured Azami-chan would reset the password,

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:19.840
to let us enter easily if she sneaked into here.

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:23.640
As expected of a common-sense girl.

00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:32.780
According to Azami's information,

00:11:32.780 --> 00:11:35.240
guards will pass through here once every two minutes.

00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:39.600
That means we have to break through here in that interval.

00:11:39.600 --> 00:11:42.150
I have seen this mechanism before.

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:47.720
In The Shinobis' 39th installment: A Shinobi's Infiltration.

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:52.760
I remember that Denzou-san sneaked into a Westerner's house, where he met a similar kind of setup.

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:57.950
Only because of one falling hair of one of his comrades who had long forelocks...

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:13.010
We must proceed with caution.

00:12:14.770 --> 00:12:18.500
If we interfere with those laser beams, we will become like beehives because of those guns.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:22.510
But, the middle is wide open.

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:33.720
Excuse me, sir.

00:12:34.360 --> 00:12:36.130
W-W-What?

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:37.980
What problem do you have with me?

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:40.350
I-I even have the invitation card.

00:12:40.350 --> 00:12:42.250
It's not what you think it is.

00:12:42.250 --> 00:12:45.210
Honored guest, please come to the VIP room.

00:12:46.610 --> 00:12:47.950
VIP room?

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:12.830
A guard has returned!

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:14.240
Himawari, hurry up!

00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:19.380
Crap!

00:13:20.530 --> 00:13:22.010
A drop of sweat...!

00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:49.220
Thanks, Momota.

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:52.470
Himawari, hurry.

00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:53.640
Yes.

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:14.990
So dark.

00:14:14.990 --> 00:14:16.470
So this is the VIP room?

00:14:16.470 --> 00:14:19.840
What about the food?

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:21.740
Sorry to have made you wait.

00:14:21.740 --> 00:14:23.540
W-What?

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:29.310
Our company has put in great effort in various research and development,

00:14:29.310 --> 00:14:33.640
aiming to eradicate viruses and illness that threaten human society.

00:14:33.820 --> 00:14:35.860
As a result,

00:14:35.860 --> 00:14:39.780
by data analysis of base pair arrangements in genetic codes of various living beings,

00:14:39.780 --> 00:14:47.360
we have been able to successfully produce exceptionally superior artificial DNA now.

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:52.660
Research on clinical applications that were not previously feasible...

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:58.280
...are now presented to everyone today.

00:14:55.480 --> 00:14:58.270
I-I have gone to the wrong place.

00:14:58.270 --> 00:14:59.610
I-I'm going home.

00:15:05.870 --> 00:15:07.850
Where exactly is Azami?

00:15:07.850 --> 00:15:08.620
Be quiet!

00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:24.360
This is quite noisy for the wailing of a perverted peeping tom.

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:26.410
A mobile surveillance camera?

00:15:26.410 --> 00:15:28.130
Stupid Himeji!

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:30.380
Anyway, let's run for it.

00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:34.140
Intruders!

00:15:34.140 --> 00:15:37.600
The security system on the eighth floor issued an emergency!

00:15:46.030 --> 00:15:48.720
I have no clue at all of where the exit is.

00:15:49.110 --> 00:15:51.100
Anyway, let's try to find it.

00:15:56.400 --> 00:16:00.230
Too much running around makes me lose my sense of direction.

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:05.450
But we can move around freely in here like him.

00:16:05.450 --> 00:16:08.320
What a lame mask that man has.

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:10.500
Yeah, weird guy.

00:16:11.550 --> 00:16:15.300
And wearing a familiar lame shirt, too.

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:19.530
Looking closer, it looks like the food is going to fall out of his pockets.

00:16:20.130 --> 00:16:22.260
That weird guy is Hayato-dono!

00:16:22.610 --> 00:16:23.990
Hayato?

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:27.930
He's Hayato-dono.

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:31.240
That mask is...

00:16:32.150 --> 00:16:37.440
The one he wore during his part-time job at the Uha Festival.

00:16:39.550 --> 00:16:40.620
Huh?

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:42.110
Hayato-dono...

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:44.260
...is gone.

00:16:47.890 --> 00:16:51.280
Looks like I'm lost...

00:17:03.130 --> 00:17:05.060
That's Takechi-sensei!

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:14.540
That's the man who spoke to the Principal.

00:17:15.770 --> 00:17:18.780
For some reason it looks bad.

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:30.910
Looks like we are trapped.

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:35.780
They've come!

00:17:37.100 --> 00:17:38.650
They're here!

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:41.770
Bye bye!

00:17:45.440 --> 00:17:46.170
Every floor.

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:48.160
They got into elevator N-35.

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:56.930
I will give more detailed information to those who are interested in collaborating on this project.

00:18:00.950 --> 00:18:02.190
Intruders?

00:18:04.880 --> 00:18:07.130
The party has turned sour.

00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:19.500
W-What the-

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:27.390
Close the emergency doors!

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:42.960
Even here?

00:18:50.720 --> 00:18:52.470
Don't breathe in those! Get down!

00:18:58.370 --> 00:18:59.650
No!

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:05.870
komurasaki-kun!

00:19:07.150 --> 00:19:08.900
Even though I told you not to worry.

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:11.170
Quickly, come here!

00:19:20.530 --> 00:19:22.060
Thank you, Komurasaki-kun.

00:19:22.060 --> 00:19:22.910
Are you okay?

00:19:23.730 --> 00:19:26.310
It's fine. I am still young.

00:19:27.510 --> 00:19:29.660
That has nothing to do with it.

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:31.580
Over there!

00:19:31.580 --> 00:19:32.420
They are here again!

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:34.090
This way!

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:04.750
Azami-chan!

00:20:05.580 --> 00:20:08.650
What are you doing in that lame suit?

00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:12.610
If I'm disguised as one of them,
wouldn't it be easier to move around?

00:20:12.610 --> 00:20:14.660
The part of being attacked was also an act?

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:17.950
No. That's...

00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:19.820
Well. I will continue surveying.

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:21.350
Got it.

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:27.970
Who are you?!

00:20:34.110 --> 00:20:36.640
It's a model that was about to be exhibited.

00:20:36.640 --> 00:20:39.880
But thanks to it, I found out a lot of things.

00:20:40.570 --> 00:20:42.340
According to my information,

00:20:42.340 --> 00:20:46.110
the place where the boy students are held is just ahead.

00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:53.940
H-Hey!

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:15.960
What? What the-

00:21:18.860 --> 00:21:19.960
Hayato-dono!

00:21:22.120 --> 00:21:23.460
What are you girls doing?

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:50.590
Here it goes!

00:22:01.140 --> 00:22:03.440
Looks like we're safe.

00:22:03.440 --> 00:22:07.290
Aren't my spy-tools handy?

00:22:07.290 --> 00:22:09.430
When did you do this?

00:22:11.520 --> 00:22:14.240
Never mind that, hold on tight!

00:22:23.870 --> 00:22:24.440
That's...

00:22:24.980 --> 00:22:27.860
That's Takechi-sensei's real face.

00:22:42.200 --> 00:22:45.420
Why was Takechi-sensei there?

00:24:11.240 --> 00:24:13.290
Tsubaki-san finally visits again.

00:24:13.290 --> 00:24:15.390
He is an old enemy of Hayato-dono.

00:24:15.390 --> 00:24:18.900
But it looks like he was attacked by something on his way to the Village of Mist.

00:24:19.370 --> 00:24:22.310
A sudden school break with all the teachers gone,

00:24:22.790 --> 00:24:24.710
what on earth is happening?

00:24:24.710 --> 00:24:26.180
But a duel...

00:24:26.180 --> 00:24:27.370
Wait, Tsubaki-san.

00:24:27.380 --> 00:24:30.880
We have no intention to fight at all.

00:24:31.230 --> 00:24:32.170
Next time:

00:24:32.170 --> 00:24:35.010
"Alternative? The bonds of fate between master and servant."

00:24:35.530 --> 00:24:39.010
Hayato-dono. Please be clear on which one you choose.
